## Handoff Execution Reference

Operational only — how to apply a pasted advisor handoff block against the prod API. Fill from your
own setup; keep secrets (passwords, tokens) out of the committed example.

- **Host / access**: how you reach the running API (e.g. SSH to the box, curl `localhost:8000`).
- **Auth**: how you mint/obtain a bearer token (the repo has a mint-token flow — see CLAUDE.local.md).
  All `/api/v1/*` endpoints need `Authorization: Bearer <token>`.
- **Action → API mapping**: table of advisor action types → HTTP method + endpoint + key body fields
  (`ADD_ALERT`, `MODIFY_ALERT`, `ADD_TO_WATCHLIST`, `ADD_RATIO`, `ADD_CALENDAR_EVENT`, `LOG_TRADE`,
  `ADD_TRIGGER`, `RETIRE_TRIGGER`, …).
- **Execution pattern**: authenticate → GET-to-resolve-IDs-by-name (match alert names by prefix, flag
  on 0/>1 matches) → execute in dependency order → report IDs → POST an execution receipt to
  `/api/v1/export/handoff-receipts` → clean up the token.
- **Current watchlist IDs**: your own `id → name` table.
- **Known bugs to avoid**: e.g. #48 percent alerts ignore `comparison_period`; #49 forex symbols don't
  resolve in ratios (use ETF proxies). Mirror the live list in AGENTS.md § gotchas.

